/-!
# Branch data for the elementary fixed-mask bound

The negative spine successively removes every nonidentity vertex. Its positive
branches restrict to commuting actors and their common fixed masks. The order
of an elementary subgroup is a power of two, which sharpens the actor count at
leaves. All branch computations are checked in the `TreeCheck` modules.
The finite data retain the literal max1 action; see `Finite.Data` for provenance.
-/
@[expose] public noncomputable section
namespace Janko4.TwoRank.Finite
